KADE HARPER — IDENTITY CANON (Tier-1)

## I. Core Identity
- **Name:** Kade Harper :contentReference[oaicite:27]{index=27}
- **Origin:** Bristol, UK :contentReference[oaicite:28]{index=28}
- **Heritage (locked current path):** British-Ghanaian :contentReference[oaicite:29]{index=29}
- **Role Function:** narrative vector; **MT successor**; truth amplifier under pressure :contentReference[oaicite:30]{index=30}
- **Trilogy Role:** Neon catalyst → Loom fracture → redemption carrier :contentReference[oaicite:31]{index=31}

## II. Cultural Origin & Early Imprint
- **Raised in:** Bristol’s protest-music / spoken-word ecosystem; community arts + youth collectives + documentary crews :contentReference[oaicite:32]{index=32}
- **Cultural imprint statement:** “If I speak honestly enough, I can stop the harm.” :contentReference[oaicite:33]{index=33}

## III. Family Structure & Emotional Ecology
- **Mother:** Ama Mensah — community arts organizer; heart-first ethics :contentReference[oaicite:34]{index=34}
- **Father:** Lewis Harper — documentary filmmaker; loving but unreliable :contentReference[oaicite:35]{index=35}
- **Core wound:** “People leave. If I don’t matter, they won’t stay.” :contentReference[oaicite:36]{index=36}

## IV. Socioeconomic Position
- **Implied ecosystem:** post-industrial port city with class division and economic precarity; voice/resistance culture forms survival logic :contentReference[oaicite:37]{index=37}

## V. Pre-Saga State
- Directionless but searching; following Tahl’s investigations obsessively; feels “called” toward New Orleans without understanding why; arrives raw and sincere :contentReference[oaicite:38]{index=38}

## VI. Psychological Architecture (Identity Loop)
- **Core traits (compressed):** emotionally perceptive; volatile but sincere; fearless in speech; deeply empathetic; impulsive under pressure :contentReference[oaicite:39]{index=39}
- **Stress patterns:** over-identification with causes; righteousness escalation; narrative obsession; self-sacrifice loops :contentReference[oaicite:40]{index=40}
- **Vulnerability hook:** susceptible to certainty-offering figures :contentReference[oaicite:41]{index=41}

## VII. MT Alignment Context (Non-Mystical)
- MT sensitivity manifests as emotional pattern recognition through story; clarity spikes while consuming Tahl’s work; intuitive grasp of narrative pressure :contentReference[oaicite:42]{index=42}

## VIII. Trilogy Anchor Facts (Identity-Relevant)
- **Neon:** idealism → misinterpretation → influence → fracture :contentReference[oaicite:43]{index=43}
- **Loom:** manipulated by Brightbreak; nearly weaponized; stopped by Tahl’s echo; forced toward responsibility over righteousness :contentReference[oaicite:44]{index=44}
- **Canon constraints:** does not ascend; cannot replace Tahl; must learn restraint; power is human-scale :contentReference[oaicite:45]{index=45}

## IX. Canon Conflict Ledger (Preserved Record)
The following legacy variants exist in source materials and are retained as historical drift (superseded by the locked current path above unless you explicitly re-open):
- **Alt ethnicity line:** “Mixed-race (South Asian + White British)” :contentReference[oaicite:46]{index=46}
- **Alt household detail set:** Easton/St. Paul’s listed as neighborhood options; household warmth inconsistent; creativity encouraged by one parent and discouraged by the other :contentReference[oaicite:47]{index=47}

END — KADE HARPER IDENTITY CANON

LACUNA — IDENTITY CANON (Tier-1)
I. Core Identity
	•	Name: Lacuna (primary usage) :contentReference[oaicite:48]{index=48}
	•	Role Function (identity-level): ritual listener; liminal stabilizer; truth interpreter :contentReference[oaicite:49]{index=49}
	•	Hard framing: not mystical; always human; master of emotional pattern recognition :contentReference[oaicite:50]{index=50}
II. Geographic Origin
	•	City: New Orleans, Louisiana (only correct origin) :contentReference[oaicite:51]{index=51}
	•	Neighborhood context: Bywater → Marigny / 7th Ward adjacency; working-class, artistic, culturally mixed; carnival-adjacent micro-economies :contentReference[oaicite:52]{index=52}
	•	Household environment: semi-nomadic, performance-adjacent, improvisational; money inconsistent; affection sideways; extended kin + chosen family blur :contentReference[oaicite:53]{index=53}
III. Cultural Origin / Heritage
	•	Ethnicity: Black Creole (mixed diasporic ancestry) with likely strands of African American, Creole of Color, French/Caribbean influence; possible distant Indigenous Louisiana ancestry :contentReference[oaicite:54]{index=54}
	•	Cultural soundscape imprint: second-line rhythms; brass bleed; spoken ritual language; Afro-Caribbean textures; Creole/Bayou storytelling; street performers; carnival-season micro-economies :contentReference[oaicite:55]{index=55}
IV. Socioeconomic Position
	•	Class position: working poor → subsistence → gig-driven survival :contentReference[oaicite:56]{index=56}
	•	Household stability: low material stability; medium emotional stability; high cultural stability :contentReference[oaicite:57]{index=57}
	•	Institutional proximity: minimal; grows up outside institutions; distrust of bureaucratic authority; learns through community and observation :contentReference[oaicite:58]{index=58}
V. Family Structure & Emotional Ecology
	•	Mother: Marianne “Miri” Baptiste — drifting presence; street performer → make-up artist → carnival crew assistant; culturally “superstitious” (not magical) :contentReference[oaicite:59]{index=59}
	•	Father: unknown or inconsistent presence; treated as a gap, not dramatized trauma :contentReference[oaicite:60]{index=60}
	•	Grandmother / Great-Aunt (anchor):Eulalie Baptiste — matriarch; keeper of stories; teaches ritual as emotional organization, not magic; teaches room-reading and pattern listening :contentReference[oaicite:61]{index=61}
	•	Siblings: none, or “fictive siblings” from performance circuit :contentReference[oaicite:62]{index=62}
VI. Social Constellation (Pre-Saga)
	•	Friends cluster: artists, performers, bartenders, gig workers; she is the “listener / watcher” people confess to; deep but transient bonds :contentReference[oaicite:63]{index=63}
	•	Off-screen anchors (optional depth): “Trick” (street magician/performer), “June” (bartender friend) :contentReference[oaicite:64]{index=64}
VII. Formative Imprints (Identity-Level)
	•	Second-line baptism (age ~6–8): learns crowds have moods and pressure patterns :contentReference[oaicite:65]{index=65}
	•	Carnival season survival (age ~10–12):hustles small jobs; improvisation and odds-handling :contentReference[oaicite:66]{index=66}
	•	Storm-season evacuation ritual (age ~11–13): pressure as weather pattern (not catastrophic) :contentReference[oaicite:67]{index=67}
VIII. Adult Operating Principle (Identity Synthesis)
	•	Raised in rhythmic chaos of New Orleans street + carnival circuits; survives by listening to people/pressure/sound/odds (not spirits); moves with ritual grace, humor, quiet acuity; becomes stabilizing force for Concord—especially for Kade—during collapse :contentReference[oaicite:68]{index=68}
